PathwayData.put("data/grammar_vocabulary/units/L06U3.json",{"strand":"grammar_vocabulary","level":6,"cefr":"B1b","unit":3,"theme":"Healthy Body, Healthy Mind","essential_question":"Which daily habits keep our bodies and minds healthy?","lessons":[{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS1","title":"I Enjoy Walking, I Decided to Start: Gerunds and Infinitives","objectives":["Students will be able to use the -ing form after verbs like enjoy, avoid and finish.","Students will be able to use the to-infinitive after verbs like decide, hope and promise, and after verb + object (advise someone to…).","I can say \"I enjoy walking\" and \"I've decided to drink more water.\"","I can say \"The doctor advised me to rest.\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام صيغة -ing بعد أفعال مثل enjoy وavoid وfinish.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام المصدر بـ to بعد أفعال مثل decide وhope وpromise، وبعد الفعل والمفعول (advise someone to…).","أستطيع أن أقول I enjoy walking وI've decided to drink more water.","أستطيع أن أقول The doctor advised me to rest."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"nutrition","pos":"noun","ipa":"/nuˈtrɪʃən/","definition":"the food your body needs to grow and stay healthy","arabic":"التغذية","example":"Good nutrition helps you concentrate in class.","image_id":"GV-L06-U3-LS1-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U3-LS1-W01"},{"word":"balanced","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈbælənst/","definition":"with the right amounts of different things","arabic":"متوازن","example":"A balanced diet includes fruit, vegetables and protein.","image_id":"GV-L06-U3-LS1-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U3-LS1-W02"},{"word":"habit","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈhæbət/","definition":"something you do often, usually without thinking","arabic":"عادة","example":"Brushing your teeth twice a day is a good habit.","image_id":"GV-L06-U3-LS1-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U3-LS1-W03"},{"word":"stress","pos":"noun","ipa":"/strɛs/","definition":"a feeling of worry because of problems or pressure","arabic":"توتّر / ضغط نفسي","example":"Exams can cause stress.","image_id":"GV-L06-U3-LS1-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U3-LS1-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"Some verbs are followed by the -ing form (gerund): enjoy, avoid, finish, keep, mind, give up, suggest, practice, miss: I enjoy walking. She avoids eating fast food. (NOT (not: enjoy to walk))\nOther verbs are followed by the to-infinitive: want, decide, hope, promise, agree, plan, learn, refuse, need, would like: I decided to drink more water. He refused to eat vegetables.\nSome verbs take an object + to-infinitive: advise, tell, ask, want, help, encourage: The doctor advised me to rest. My mother wants me to sleep early. A few verbs (like, love, hate, start, begin) can take both with little difference: I love swimming / I love to swim.\nenjoy / avoid / finish / keep / mind / give up / suggest + -ing\nwant / decide / hope / promise / agree / plan / learn / refuse + to + base verb\nadvise / tell / ask / encourage + object + to + base verb\nlike / love / hate / start / begin → -ing or to (both OK)","examples":["My father gave up drinking soda last year.","We plan to cycle to school next term.","Do you mind opening the window?","I learned to cook healthy meals from my grandmother.","Faisal keeps forgetting his water bottle.","The nurse told me to rest for two days.","She avoids eating late at night.","I hope to run five kilometers by the summer."],"common_errors":["✗ I enjoy to swim. → ✓ I enjoy swimming. (enjoy + -ing.)","✗ I decided going to the gym. → ✓ I decided to go to the gym. (decide + to.)","✗ The doctor advised me rest. → ✓ The doctor advised me to rest. (advise + object + to.)","✗ I want that you help me. → ✓ I want you to help me. (want + object + to (not that).)"],"arabic":"بعض الأفعال يأتي بعدها الفعل بصيغة ing مثل enjoy وavoid وfinish وkeep وmind: I enjoy walking.\nوبعضها يأتي بعده to + المصدر مثل want وdecide وhope وpromise وagree: I decided to drink more water.\nadvise وtell وask وencourage يأتي بعدها مفعول ثم to: The doctor advised me to rest.\nفي العربية نقول «أريد أن تساعدني»، أما في الإنجليزية فنقول I want you to help me (وليس I want that you help me)."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “I Enjoy Walking, I Decided to Start: Gerunds and Infinitives”. Let’s learn verb + -ing (enjoy, avoid, finish, keep, mind, give up, suggest); verb + to-infinitive (want, decide, hope, promise, agree, plan, learn, refuse); verb + object + to-infinitive (advise, tell, ask) together.","on_screen":"GV-L06-U3-LS1 | I Enjoy Walking, I Decided to Start: Gerunds and Infinitives","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Listen to the start of “Sara's Healthy Habits Challenge”: Last month, our class started a \"Healthy Habits Challenge,\" and I decided to take part. I really enjoy eating sweets, so I knew it wasn't going to be easy! Look at the green words.","on_screen":"Last month, our class started a \"Healthy Habits Challenge,\" and I decided to take part. I really enjoy eating sweets, so I knew it wasn't going to be easy!","visual":"Image GV-L06-U3-LS1-IMG01 animates gently; target words glow Leaf Green as they are spoken."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Some verbs are followed by the -ing form (gerund): enjoy, avoid, finish, keep, mind, give up, suggest, practice, miss: I enjoy walking. She avoids eating fast food. (NOT (not: enjoy to walk)) Other verbs are followed by the to-infinitive: want, decide, hope, promise, agree, plan, learn, refuse, need, would like: I decided to drink more water. He refused to eat vegetables.","on_screen":"enjoy / avoid / finish / keep / mind / give up / suggest + -ing • want / decide / hope / promise / agree / plan / learn / refuse + to + base verb • advise / tell / ask / encourage + object + to + base verb","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. My father gave up drinking soda last year. We plan to cycle to school next term. Do you mind opening the window?","on_screen":"My father gave up drinking soda last year. / We plan to cycle to school next term. / Do you mind opening the window?","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I enjoy to swim.” That’s not right. We say: “I enjoy swimming.” enjoy + -ing.","on_screen":"✗ I enjoy to swim.   ✓ I enjoy swimming.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"I enjoy to walk\" or \"I enjoy walking\"? … Think! … *I enjoy walking*. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"I enjoy walking\" and \"I've decided to drink more water.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"I enjoy walking\" and \"I've decided to drink more water.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: verb + -ing (enjoy, avoid, finish, keep, mind, give up, suggest); verb + to-infinitive (want, decide, hope, promise, agree, plan, learn, refuse); verb + object + to-infinitive (advise, tell, ask).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","بعض الأفعال يأتي بعدها الفعل بصيغة ing مثل enjoy وavoid وfinish وkeep وmind: I enjoy walking.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I enjoy to swim. — الصحيح: I enjoy swimming.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول I enjoy walking وI've decided to drink more water."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Sara's Healthy Habits Challenge","body":"Last month, our class started a \"Healthy Habits Challenge,\" and I decided to take part.\nI really enjoy eating sweets, so I knew it wasn't going to be easy! First, I promised to drink eight glasses of water a day. I also agreed to avoid eating fast food during the week.\nMy mother suggested going for a walk after dinner, so now we walk together around the park every evening. At first, I hated walking in the heat, but now I love it.\nOur teacher, Ms. Huda, advised us to sleep at least eight hours. I used to keep checking my phone in bed, but I've given that up. Now I finish reading a chapter of my book and switch off the light at ten.\nThe hardest part was learning to say no to my favorite cookies! I didn't want to give up sweets completely, so I decided to have them only on weekends.\nAfter four weeks, I feel more energetic, and I don't mind waking up early anymore. I hope to continue these habits all year.","word_count":177,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U3-LS1-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"I enjoy ___ in the sea in summer.","options":["swam","swimming","swim","to swim"],"answer":"swimming","explanation":"enjoy / avoid / finish / keep / mind / give up / suggest + -ing.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال + ing."},{"q":"My uncle has decided ___ smoking.","options":["quit","quitting","to quitting","to quit"],"answer":"to quit","explanation":"want / decide / hope / promise / agree / plan / learn + to.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال + to."},{"q":"Please avoid ___ sugary drinks before bed.","options":["have","having","had","to have"],"answer":"having","explanation":"enjoy / avoid / finish / keep / mind / give up / suggest + -ing.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال + ing."},{"q":"The doctor advised my grandfather ___ more.","options":["walk","walks","to walk","walking"],"answer":"to walk","explanation":"advise / tell / ask / want + object + to.","explanation_ar":"الفعل + مفعول + to."},{"q":"We hope ___ the school health quiz this year.","options":["win","to winning","to win","winning"],"answer":"to win","explanation":"want / decide / hope / promise / agree / plan / learn + to.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال + to."},{"q":"My little sister started ___ when she was four.","options":["reading","read","reads","readed"],"answer":"reading","explanation":"like / love / hate / start / begin → -ing or to.","explanation_ar":"الصيغتان صحيحتان."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS1-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Complete with the -ing form or the to-infinitive. Word bank: to stretch, to help, waiting","items":[{"q":"Do you mind ______ (wait) for five minutes?","options":[],"answer":"waiting","explanation":"enjoy / avoid / finish / keep / mind / give up / suggest + -ing.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال + ing."},{"q":"My brother promised ______ (help) me with my diet plan.","options":[],"answer":"to help","explanation":"want / decide / hope / promise / agree / plan / learn + to.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال + to."},{"q":"The coach told us ______ (stretch) before every match.","options":[],"answer":"to stretch","explanation":"advise / tell / ask / want + object + to.","explanation_ar":"الفعل + مفعول + to."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS1-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the mistake.","items":[{"q":"I finished to do my exercises at seven.","options":[],"answer":"I finished doing my exercises at seven.","explanation":"to do → doing. enjoy / avoid / finish / keep / mind / give up / suggest + -ing.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: to do → doing. الأفعال + ing."},{"q":"She refused eating the fried chicken.","options":[],"answer":"She refused to eat the fried chicken.","explanation":"eating → to eat. want / decide / hope / promise / agree / plan / learn + to.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: eating → to eat. الأفعال + to."},{"q":"My mother wants that I sleep before ten.","options":[],"answer":"My mother wants me to sleep before ten.","explanation":"that I sleep → me to sleep. advise / tell / ask / want + object + to.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: that I sleep → me to sleep. الفعل + مفعول + to."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS1-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Write about your habits.","items":[{"q":"Something you enjoy doing in your free time: ___","options":[],"answer":"I enjoy playing basketball with my friends.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses verb + -ing (enjoy, avoid, finish, keep, mind, give up, suggest); verb + to-infinitive (want, decide, hope, promise, agree, plan, learn, refuse); verb + object + to-infinitive (advise, tell, ask) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something you've decided to do this year: ___","options":[],"answer":"I've decided to eat more vegetables.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses verb + -ing (enjoy, avoid, finish, keep, mind, give up, suggest); verb + to-infinitive (want, decide, hope, promise, agree, plan, learn, refuse); verb + object + to-infinitive (advise, tell, ask) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something you avoid doing before bed: ___","options":[],"answer":"I avoid using my phone before bed.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses verb + -ing (enjoy, avoid, finish, keep, mind, give up, suggest); verb + to-infinitive (want, decide, hope, promise, agree, plan, learn, refuse); verb + object + to-infinitive (advise, tell, ask) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something you hope to achieve: ___","options":[],"answer":"I hope to run a 10 km race.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses verb + -ing (enjoy, avoid, finish, keep, mind, give up, suggest); verb + to-infinitive (want, decide, hope, promise, agree, plan, learn, refuse); verb + object + to-infinitive (advise, tell, ask) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something a doctor or parent advised you to do: ___","options":[],"answer":"My mother advised me to drink more water.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses verb + -ing (enjoy, avoid, finish, keep, mind, give up, suggest); verb + to-infinitive (want, decide, hope, promise, agree, plan, learn, refuse); verb + object + to-infinitive (advise, tell, ask) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS1-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: My healthy habits challenge.","items":[{"q":"Write 3 sentences about habits you want to change with decide, promise and plan.","options":[],"answer":"I've decided to sleep earlier. I promise to walk every day. I plan to eat fruit for snacks.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses verb + -ing (enjoy, avoid, finish, keep, mind, give up, suggest); verb + to-infinitive (want, decide, hope, promise, agree, plan, learn, refuse); verb + object + to-infinitive (advise, tell, ask) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences with enjoy and avoid.","options":[],"answer":"I enjoy cooking healthy salads. I avoid drinking soda.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses verb + -ing (enjoy, avoid, finish, keep, mind, give up, suggest); verb + to-infinitive (want, decide, hope, promise, agree, plan, learn, refuse); verb + object + to-infinitive (advise, tell, ask) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence with advise / tell + object + to.","options":[],"answer":"My coach told me to drink water during training.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses verb + -ing (enjoy, avoid, finish, keep, mind, give up, suggest); verb + to-infinitive (want, decide, hope, promise, agree, plan, learn, refuse); verb + object + to-infinitive (advise, tell, ask) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Grammar Hot Seat","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["One student from each team sits in the hot seat facing the class.","The teacher shows a cue card behind the student; the team gives a clue using verb + -ing (enjoy, avoid, finish, keep, mind, give up, suggest); verb + to-infinitive (want, decide, hope, promise, agree, plan, learn, refuse); verb + object + to-infinitive (advise, tell, ask) without saying the word.","The student in the hot seat guesses the cue word within 30 seconds.","Teams score 1 point for a correct guess and 1 point for a correct clue sentence. Rotate seats."],"data":[{"label":"I enjoy…"},{"label":"I avoid…"},{"label":"I've decided to…"},{"label":"I hope to…"},{"label":"I don't mind…"},{"label":"I want to…"},{"label":"I'm good at…"},{"label":"I'm looking forward to…"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"My grandfather keeps ___ about his old football days.","options":["talk","talked","to talk","talking"],"answer":"talking","explanation":"enjoy / avoid / finish / keep / mind / give up / suggest + -ing.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال + ing."},{"q":"I've learned ___ healthy meals from YouTube.","options":["cooking","to cooking","to cook","cook"],"answer":"to cook","explanation":"want / decide / hope / promise / agree / plan / learn + to.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال + to."},{"q":"","options":["Have you finished eat your lunch?","Have you finished to eat your lunch?","Have you finished eating your lunch?","Have you finished to eating your lunch?"],"answer":"Have you finished eating your lunch?","explanation":"enjoy / avoid / finish / keep / mind / give up / suggest + -ing.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال + ing."},{"q":"","options":["The nurse asked me to roll up my sleeve.","The nurse asked me rolling up my sleeve.","The nurse asked me roll up my sleeve.","The nurse asked to me roll up my sleeve."],"answer":"The nurse asked me to roll up my sleeve.","explanation":"advise / tell / ask / want + object + to.","explanation_ar":"الفعل + مفعول + to."},{"q":"My friends suggested ___ a picnic in the park.","options":["having","had","to have","have"],"answer":"having","explanation":"enjoy / avoid / finish / keep / mind / give up / suggest + -ing.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال + ing."},{"q":"We agreed ___ to the gym together three times a week.","options":["go","to going","going","to go"],"answer":"to go","explanation":"want / decide / hope / promise / agree / plan / learn + to.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال + to."},{"q":"","options":["I don't mind to getting up early for Fajr.","I don't mind getting up early for Fajr.","I don't mind to get up early for Fajr.","I don't mind get up early for Fajr."],"answer":"I don't mind getting up early for Fajr.","explanation":"enjoy / avoid / finish / keep / mind / give up / suggest + -ing.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال + ing."},{"q":"My parents encouraged me ___ the swimming team.","options":["joining","to join","to joining","join"],"answer":"to join","explanation":"advise / tell / ask / want + object + to.","explanation_ar":"الفعل + مفعول + to."},{"q":"Which verb can be followed by both \"-ing\" and \"to\"?","options":["love","decide","enjoy","avoid"],"answer":"love","explanation":"like / love / hate / start / begin → -ing or to.","explanation_ar":"الصيغتان صحيحتان."},{"q":"Rakan refused ___ the medicine because it tasted bad.","options":["take","taking","to taking","to take"],"answer":"to take","explanation":"want / decide / hope / promise / agree / plan / learn + to.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال + to."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS1-IMG01","prompt":"Sara's \"Healthy Habits Challenge\" chart on her bedroom wall with stickers: water glasses, a walking shoe, a moon for sleep, and a crossed-out burger; Sara walking in a park at sunset with her mother. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Sara's \"Healthy Habits Challenge\" chart on her bedroom wall with stickers: water glasses, a walking shoe, a moon for sleep, and a crossed-out burger; Sara walking in a park at sunset with her mother"},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS1-IMG02","prompt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about verb + -ing (enjoy, avoid, finish, keep, mind, give up, suggest); verb + to-infinitive (want, decide, hope, promise, agree, plan, learn, refuse); verb + object + to-infinitive (advise, tell, ask), with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right; leave large empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about verb + -ing (enjoy, avoid, finish, keep, mind, give up, suggest)"},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS1-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows nutrition (the food your body needs to grow and stay healthy); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing nutrition: the food your body needs to grow and stay healthy"},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS1-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows balanced (with the right amounts of different things); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing balanced: with the right amounts of different things"},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS1-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows habit (something you do often, usually without thinking); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing habit: something you do often, usually without thinking"},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS1-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows stress (a feeling of worry because of problems or pressure); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing stress: a feeling of worry because of problems or pressure"},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS1-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Grammar Hot Seat”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Grammar Hot Seat"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U3-LS1-W01","script":"nutrition. nutrition. Good nutrition helps you concentrate in class.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U3-LS1-W02","script":"balanced. balanced. A balanced diet includes fruit, vegetables and protein.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U3-LS1-W03","script":"habit. habit. Brushing your teeth twice a day is a good habit.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U3-LS1-W04","script":"stress. stress. Exams can cause stress.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U3-LS1-T1","script":"Last month, our class started a \"Healthy Habits Challenge,\" and I decided to take part. I really enjoy eating sweets, so I knew it wasn't going to be easy! First, I promised to drink eight glasses of water a day. I also agreed to avoid eating fast food during the week. My mother suggested going for a walk after dinner, so now we walk together around the park every evening. At first, I hated walking in the heat, but now I love it. Our teacher, Ms. Huda, advised us to sleep at least eight hours. I used to keep checking my phone in bed, but I've given that up. Now I finish reading a chapter of my book and switch off the light at ten. The hardest part was learning to say no to my favorite cookies! I didn't want to give up sweets completely, so I decided to have them only on weekends. After four weeks, I feel more energetic, and I don't mind waking up early anymore. I hope to continue these habits all year.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U3-LS1-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “I Enjoy Walking, I Decided to Start: Gerunds and Infinitives”. Let’s learn verb + -ing (enjoy, avoid, finish, keep, mind, give up, suggest); verb + to-infinitive (want, decide, hope, promise, agree, plan, learn, refuse); verb + object + to-infinitive (advise, tell, ask) together. Listen to the start of “Sara's Healthy Habits Challenge”: Last month, our class started a \"Healthy Habits Challenge,\" and I decided to take part. I really enjoy eating sweets, so I knew it wasn't going to be easy! Look at the green words. Some verbs are followed by the -ing form (gerund): enjoy, avoid, finish, keep, mind, give up, suggest, practice, miss: I enjoy walking. She avoids eating fast food. (NOT (not: enjoy to walk)) Other verbs are followed by the to-infinitive: want, decide, hope, promise, agree, plan, learn, refuse, need, would like: I decided to drink more water. He refused to eat vegetables. Here are some examples. My father gave up drinking soda last year. We plan to cycle to school next term. Do you mind opening the window? Be careful! Some learners say: “I enjoy to swim.” That’s not right. We say: “I enjoy swimming.” enjoy + -ing. Quick check: \"I enjoy to walk\" or \"I enjoy walking\"? … Think! … *I enjoy walking*. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"I enjoy walking\" and \"I've decided to drink more water.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.95"}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS2","title":"Exercising Is Fun: Gerunds as Subjects and after Prepositions","objectives":["Students will be able to use the -ing form as the subject of a sentence.","Students will be able to use the -ing form after prepositions, including look forward to.","I can say \"Eating vegetables is good for you.\"","I can say \"I'm good at cooking\" and \"I'm looking forward to seeing you.\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام صيغة -ing فاعلًا في الجملة.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام صيغة -ing بعد حروف الجر، بما في ذلك look forward to.","أستطيع أن أقول Eating vegetables is good for you.","أستطيع أن أقول I'm good at cooking وI'm looking forward to seeing you."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"exercise","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɛksɚˌsaɪz/","definition":"physical activity to stay fit and healthy","arabic":"تمارين رياضية","example":"Thirty minutes of exercise a day is enough for most people.","image_id":"GV-L06-U3-LS2-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U3-LS2-W01"},{"word":"hydrated","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈhaɪˌdreɪtəd/","definition":"having enough water in your body","arabic":"مرتوٍ (جسمه فيه ماء كافٍ)","example":"Stay hydrated in the summer heat.","image_id":"GV-L06-U3-LS2-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U3-LS2-W02"},{"word":"immune system","pos":"noun phrase","ipa":"/ˌɪˈmjun ˈsɪstəm/","definition":"the parts of the body that fight illness","arabic":"جهاز المناعة","example":"Sleep helps your immune system.","image_id":"GV-L06-U3-LS2-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U3-LS2-W03"},{"word":"protein","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈproʊˌtin/","definition":"a substance in food like meat, eggs and beans that builds muscles","arabic":"بروتين","example":"Eggs are full of protein.","image_id":"GV-L06-U3-LS2-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U3-LS2-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"The -ing form can be the subject of a sentence. It's singular, so the verb is singular: Exercising is fun. Eating too much sugar is bad for your teeth.\nAfter a preposition (at, in, of, about, for, before, after, without, instead of), always use the -ing form: I'm good at cooking. She's interested in learning first aid. Wash your hands before eating. Walk instead of taking the car.\nBe careful with to! In look forward to, be used to and get used to, to is a preposition, so it's followed by -ing: I'm looking forward to seeing you. We can also say It's + adjective + to-infinitive: It's important to sleep well. = Sleeping well is important.\n-ing as subject + singular verb: Swimming is…\npreposition + -ing: good at running, tired of waiting\nlook forward to + -ing (NOT look forward to see)\nIt's + adjective + to + base verb = -ing subject","examples":["Drinking water helps you concentrate.","Eating fast food every day is unhealthy.","My sister is good at making salads.","I'm tired of sitting at my desk all day.","Stretch before running.","He lost weight by cutting out soda.","We're looking forward to visiting the health fair.","It's hard to wake up early in winter."],"common_errors":["✗ Eat vegetables is good for you. → ✓ Eating vegetables is good for you. (Subject → -ing.)","✗ Swimming are fun. → ✓ Swimming is fun. (-ing subject → singular verb.)","✗ I'm interested in learn karate. → ✓ I'm interested in learning karate. (Preposition + -ing.)","✗ I'm looking forward to see you. → ✓ I'm looking forward to seeing you. (look forward to + -ing.)"],"arabic":"يمكن أن تكون صيغة ing فاعلًا في الجملة، ويكون الفعل بعدها مفردًا: Exercising is fun.\nبعد حروف الجر (at وin وof وbefore وafter وwithout وinstead of) نستخدم صيغة ing: I'm good at cooking.\nانتبه: to في look forward to حرف جر، لذلك نقول looking forward to seeing.\nيمكن أن نقول أيضًا: It's important to sleep well = Sleeping well is important."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Exercising Is Fun: Gerunds as Subjects and after Prepositions”. Let’s learn the -ing form as the subject of a sentence; preposition + -ing (good at, interested in, tired of, before, after, instead of, without); look forward to + -ing; It's + adjective + to-infinitive together.","on_screen":"GV-L06-U3-LS2 | Exercising Is Fun: Gerunds as Subjects and after Prepositions","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Remember these patterns: Walking every day keeps you fit. • I'm interested in joining the club. Skipping breakfast isn't a good idea. • He left without saying goodbye. Is drinking coffee bad for teenagers? • Are you good at cooking?","on_screen":"Walking every day keeps you fit. • I'm interested in joining the club. | Skipping breakfast isn't a good idea. • He left without saying goodbye. | Is drinking coffee bad for teenagers? • Are you good at cooking?","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"The -ing form can be the subject of a sentence. It's singular, so the verb is singular: Exercising is fun. Eating too much sugar is bad for your teeth. After a preposition (at, in, of, about, for, before, after, without, instead of), always use the -ing form: I'm good at cooking. She's interested in learning first aid. Wash your hands before eating. Walk instead of taking the car.","on_screen":"-ing as subject + singular verb: Swimming is… • preposition + -ing: good at running, tired of waiting • look forward to + -ing (NOT look forward to see)","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Drinking water helps you concentrate. Eating fast food every day is unhealthy. My sister is good at making salads.","on_screen":"Drinking water helps you concentrate. / Eating fast food every day is unhealthy. / My sister is good at making salads.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “Eat vegetables is good for you.” That’s not right. We say: “Eating vegetables is good for you.” Subject → -ing.","on_screen":"✗ Eat vegetables is good for you.   ✓ Eating vegetables is good for you.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"___ is good for your heart.\" swim / swimming? … Think! … *Swimming*. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"Eating vegetables is good for you.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"Eating vegetables is good for you.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: the -ing form as the subject of a sentence; preposition + -ing (good at, interested in, tired of, before, after, instead of, without); look forward to + -ing; It's + adjective + to-infinitive.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","يمكن أن تكون صيغة ing فاعلًا في الجملة، ويكون الفعل بعدها مفردًا: Exercising is fun.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: Eat vegetables is good for you. — الصحيح: Eating vegetables is good for you.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول Eating vegetables is good for you."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"___ enough water helps your body work well.","options":["Drink","To drinking","Drinking","Drinks"],"answer":"Drinking","explanation":"-ing form as the subject + singular verb.","explanation_ar":"ing فاعلًا."},{"q":"My cousin is very good at ___ healthy desserts.","options":["making","make","made","to make"],"answer":"making","explanation":"adjective + preposition + -ing (good at, tired of).","explanation_ar":"الصفة + حرف الجر + ing."},{"q":"Wash your hands before ___.","options":["ate","eating","eat","to eat"],"answer":"eating","explanation":"Preposition + -ing.","explanation_ar":"حرف الجر + ing."},{"q":"I'm looking forward to ___ my grandparents in Abha.","options":["be visit","visit","visited","visiting"],"answer":"visiting","explanation":"look forward to + -ing.","explanation_ar":"look forward to + ing."},{"q":"___ important to have a balanced breakfast.","options":["That's","Its","It's","There's"],"answer":"It's","explanation":"It's + adjective + to + base verb.","explanation_ar":"It's + صفة + to."},{"q":"Walking every day ___ your heart strong.","options":["keep","have kept","are keeping","keeps"],"answer":"keeps","explanation":"-ing form as the subject + singular verb.","explanation_ar":"ing فاعلًا."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS2-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Complete with the correct form. Word bank: learning, taking, Sleeping","items":[{"q":"______ (sleep) eight hours a night is important for teenagers.","options":[],"answer":"Sleeping","explanation":"-ing form as the subject + singular verb.","explanation_ar":"ing فاعلًا."},{"q":"Lina is interested in ______ (learn) first aid.","options":[],"answer":"learning","explanation":"adjective + preposition + -ing (good at, tired of).","explanation_ar":"الصفة + حرف الجر + ing."},{"q":"You can stay fit by ______ (take) the stairs instead of the elevator.","options":[],"answer":"taking","explanation":"Preposition + -ing.","explanation_ar":"حرف الجر + ing."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS2-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Rewrite. Use an -ing subject.","items":[{"q":"It's healthy to eat fruit every day.  (-ing subject)","options":[],"answer":"Eating fruit every day is healthy.","explanation":"It's + adjective + to + base verb.","explanation_ar":"It's + صفة + to."},{"q":"It's dangerous to swim alone.  (-ing subject)","options":[],"answer":"Swimming alone is dangerous.","explanation":"It's + adjective + to + base verb.","explanation_ar":"It's + صفة + to."},{"q":"It's relaxing to read before bed.  (-ing subject)","options":[],"answer":"Reading before bed is relaxing.","explanation":"It's + adjective + to + base verb.","explanation_ar":"It's + صفة + to."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS2-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Write about you.","items":[{"q":"Something you're good at doing: ___","options":[],"answer":"I'm good at cooking pasta.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses the -ing form as the subject of a sentence; preposition + -ing (good at, interested in, tired of, before, after, instead of, without); look forward to + -ing; It's + adjective + to-infinitive correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something you're tired of doing: ___","options":[],"answer":"I'm tired of waiting for the bus.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses the -ing form as the subject of a sentence; preposition + -ing (good at, interested in, tired of, before, after, instead of, without); look forward to + -ing; It's + adjective + to-infinitive correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something you're looking forward to doing: ___","options":[],"answer":"I'm looking forward to traveling in the summer.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses the -ing form as the subject of a sentence; preposition + -ing (good at, interested in, tired of, before, after, instead of, without); look forward to + -ing; It's + adjective + to-infinitive correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something you do instead of watching TV: ___","options":[],"answer":"I read comics instead of watching TV.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses the -ing form as the subject of a sentence; preposition + -ing (good at, interested in, tired of, before, after, instead of, without); look forward to + -ing; It's + adjective + to-infinitive correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A healthy activity and why it's good: ___","options":[],"answer":"Cycling is good because it makes your legs strong.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses the -ing form as the subject of a sentence; preposition + -ing (good at, interested in, tired of, before, after, instead of, without); look forward to + -ing; It's + adjective + to-infinitive correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS2-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Health fair posters.","items":[{"q":"Write 3 poster slogans that start with an -ing subject.","options":[],"answer":"Drinking water keeps you sharp! Walking to school saves energy! Sleeping early makes you energetic!","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses the -ing form as the subject of a sentence; preposition + -ing (good at, interested in, tired of, before, after, instead of, without); look forward to + -ing; It's + adjective + to-infinitive correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 tips with before / after / instead of + -ing.","options":[],"answer":"Stretch before playing football. Eat fruit instead of eating chips.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses the -ing form as the subject of a sentence; preposition + -ing (good at, interested in, tired of, before, after, instead of, without); look forward to + -ing; It's + adjective + to-infinitive correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence with \"It's + adjective + to\".","options":[],"answer":"It's easy to make a healthy smoothie.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses the -ing form as the subject of a sentence; preposition + -ing (good at, interested in, tired of, before, after, instead of, without); look forward to + -ing; It's + adjective + to-infinitive correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Sentence Builder Race","mechanic":"sentence_builder","rules":["Each team receives the same tile set.","In 5 minutes, build as many different correct sentences as possible using the -ing form as the subject of a sentence; preposition + -ing (good at, interested in, tired of, before, after, instead of, without); look forward to + -ing; It's + adjective + to-infinitive.","Write each sentence on the team sheet.","Swap sheets with another team to check. One point per correct sentence; no points for repeats."],"data":[{"cue":"I / enjoy / swim / in the sea"},{"cue":"she / decide / drink more water"},{"cue":"we / avoid / eat / fast food"},{"cue":"he / promise / go to bed early"},{"cue":"they / finish / do / their exercises"},{"cue":"I / hope / run / a marathon"},{"cue":"my dad / give up / drink / soda"},{"cue":"do you mind / open / the window?"},{"cue":"I / learn / cook / healthy meals"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"___ too much screen time can hurt your eyes.","options":["To having","Having","Has","Have"],"answer":"Having","explanation":"-ing form as the subject + singular verb.","explanation_ar":"ing فاعلًا."},{"q":"","options":["Cook at home is cheaper than eating out.","Cooking at home are cheaper than eating out.","Cooking at home is cheaper than eating out.","To cooking at home is cheaper than eating out."],"answer":"Cooking at home is cheaper than eating out.","explanation":"-ing form as the subject + singular verb.","explanation_ar":"ing فاعلًا."},{"q":"She left the gym without ___ her bottle.","options":["to take","taking","took","take"],"answer":"taking","explanation":"Preposition + -ing.","explanation_ar":"حرف الجر + ing."},{"q":"","options":["We're looking forward to joining the health club.","We're looking forward to join the health club.","We're looking forward for joining the health club.","We're looking forward joining the health club."],"answer":"We're looking forward to joining the health club.","explanation":"look forward to + -ing.","explanation_ar":"look forward to + ing."},{"q":"I'm afraid of ___ injections.","options":["got","get","to get","getting"],"answer":"getting","explanation":"adjective + preposition + -ing (good at, tired of).","explanation_ar":"الصفة + حرف الجر + ing."},{"q":"___ easy to forget to drink water at school.","options":["That","It","Its","It's"],"answer":"It's","explanation":"It's + adjective + to + base verb.","explanation_ar":"It's + صفة + to."},{"q":"How about ___ a fruit salad for the party?","options":["made","making","make","to make"],"answer":"making","explanation":"Preposition + -ing.","explanation_ar":"حرف الجر + ing."},{"q":"My brother is tired of ___ for the doctor.","options":["waiting","to wait","wait","waited"],"answer":"waiting","explanation":"adjective + preposition + -ing (good at, tired of).","explanation_ar":"الصفة + حرف الجر + ing."},{"q":"","options":["Skip meals isn't good for you.","Skipping meals aren't good for you.","Skipping meals isn't good for you.","To skipping meals isn't good for you."],"answer":"Skipping meals isn't good for you.","explanation":"-ing form as the subject + singular verb.","explanation_ar":"ing فاعلًا."},{"q":"Which sentence uses \"to\" as a preposition?","options":["I want to meet the dentist.","I decided to meet the dentist.","I'm looking forward to meeting the dentist.","I hope to meet the dentist."],"answer":"I'm looking forward to meeting the dentist.","explanation":"look forward to + -ing.","explanation_ar":"look forward to + ing."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS2-IMG01","prompt":"A school health fair: posters saying \"Drinking water keeps you focused!\", \"Instead of sitting all day, stretch!\", students at a cooking stand, and Yusuf with a sign \"I'm looking forward to running the school mile!\". Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A school health fair: posters saying \"Drinking water keeps you focused!\", \"Instead of sitting all day, stretch!\", students at a cooking stand, and Yusuf with a sign \"I'm looking forward to running the school mile!\""},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS2-IMG02","prompt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of the -ing form as the subject of a sentence; preposition + -ing (good at, interested in, tired of, before, after, instead of, without); look forward to + -ing; It's + adjective + to-infinitive: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “Healthy Body, Healthy Mind”; empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of the -ing form as the subject of a sentence"},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS2-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows exercise (physical activity to stay fit and healthy); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing exercise: physical activity to stay fit and healthy"},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS2-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows hydrated (having enough water in your body); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing hydrated: having enough water in your body"},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS2-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows immune system (the parts of the body that fight illness); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing immune system: the parts of the body that fight illness"},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS2-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows protein (a substance in food like meat, eggs and beans that builds muscles); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing protein: a substance in food like meat, eggs and beans that builds muscles"},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS2-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Sentence Builder Race”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Sentence Builder Race"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U3-LS2-W01","script":"exercise. exercise. Thirty minutes of exercise a day is enough for most people.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U3-LS2-W02","script":"hydrated. hydrated. Stay hydrated in the summer heat.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U3-LS2-W03","script":"immune system. immune system. Sleep helps your immune system.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U3-LS2-W04","script":"protein. protein. Eggs are full of protein.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U3-LS2-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Exercising Is Fun: Gerunds as Subjects and after Prepositions”. Let’s learn the -ing form as the subject of a sentence; preposition + -ing (good at, interested in, tired of, before, after, instead of, without); look forward to + -ing; It's + adjective + to-infinitive together. Remember these patterns: Walking every day keeps you fit. • I'm interested in joining the club. Skipping breakfast isn't a good idea. • He left without saying goodbye. Is drinking coffee bad for teenagers? • Are you good at cooking? The -ing form can be the subject of a sentence. It's singular, so the verb is singular: Exercising is fun. Eating too much sugar is bad for your teeth. After a preposition (at, in, of, about, for, before, after, without, instead of), always use the -ing form: I'm good at cooking. She's interested in learning first aid. Wash your hands before eating. Walk instead of taking the car. Here are some examples. Drinking water helps you concentrate. Eating fast food every day is unhealthy. My sister is good at making salads. Be careful! Some learners say: “Eat vegetables is good for you.” That’s not right. We say: “Eating vegetables is good for you.” Subject → -ing. Quick check: \"___ is good for your heart.\" swim / swimming? … Think! … *Swimming*. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"Eating vegetables is good for you.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.95"}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS3","title":"Under the Weather, Back on My Feet: Health Phrasal Verbs, Idioms and Word Families","objectives":["Students will be able to understand and use health phrasal verbs and idioms.","Students will be able to use health word families (health → healthy → healthily).","I can say \"I came down with a cold, but I'm back on my feet now.\"","I can choose \"healthy\" or \"healthily\" correctly."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من فهم الأفعال المركبة والتعابير الاصطلاحية الصحية واستخدامها.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام عائلات الكلمات الصحية (health → healthy → healthily).","أستطيع أن أقول I came down with a cold, but I'm back on my feet now.","أستطيع أن أختار healthy أو healthily بشكل صحيح."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"vitamin","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈvaɪtəmən/","definition":"a natural substance in food that keeps you healthy","arabic":"فيتامين","example":"Oranges contain vitamin C.","image_id":"GV-L06-U3-LS3-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U3-LS3-W01"},{"word":"posture","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈpɑstʃɚ/","definition":"the way you hold your body when you sit or stand","arabic":"وضعية الجسم","example":"Bad posture can hurt your back.","image_id":"GV-L06-U3-LS3-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U3-LS3-W02"},{"word":"mental","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈmɛntəl/","definition":"connected with the mind","arabic":"ذهني / نفسي","example":"Mental health is as important as physical health.","image_id":"GV-L06-U3-LS3-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U3-LS3-W03"},{"word":"symptom","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈsɪmptəm/","definition":"a sign of an illness","arabic":"عَرَض (للمرض)","example":"A high temperature is a symptom of the flu.","image_id":"GV-L06-U3-LS3-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U3-LS3-W04"},{"word":"recover","pos":"verb","ipa":"/rɪˈkʌvɚ/","definition":"to get better after an illness","arabic":"يتعافى","example":"It took me a week to recover from the flu.","image_id":"GV-L06-U3-LS3-W05","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U3-LS3-W05"},{"word":"energetic","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˌɛnɚˈdʒɛtɪk/","definition":"full of energy","arabic":"نشيط / مفعم بالحيوية","example":"I feel energetic after a good breakfast.","image_id":"GV-L06-U3-LS3-W06","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U3-LS3-W06"}],"explanation":{"text":"Phrasal verbs for health: cut down on (eat or use less), cut out (stop completely), get over (recover from), come down with (start to have an illness), stay up (not go to bed), pass out (become unconscious, faint).\nIdioms are phrases whose meaning is different from the words: under the weather = a little ill; back on my feet = healthy again; (as) fit as a fiddle = very healthy; take it easy = relax, don't work too hard; burn the midnight oil = study or work late at night.\nHealth word families: health (n) → healthy (adj) → healthily (adv) → unhealthy (adj); stress → stressful / stressed; energy → energetic; recover → recovery; relax → relaxation / relaxed; nutrition → nutritious.\nWord families: health: healthy (adj), healthily (adv) | stress: stressful (adj), stressed (adj) | energy: energetic (adj), energize (v) | recover: recovery (n) | relax: relaxation (n), relaxed (adj) | nutrition: nutritious (adj)","examples":["I'm trying to cut down on sugar.","My dad cut out fried food completely.","It took me two weeks to get over the flu.","My sister came down with a cold before her exam.","Don't stay up too late on school nights.","I'm feeling a bit under the weather today.","After a week in bed, Omar was back on his feet.","Dates are a nutritious snack."],"common_errors":["✗ I want to cut down sugar. → ✓ I want to cut down on sugar. (cut down on + noun.)","✗ I'm under the weathers. → ✓ I'm under the weather. (Idioms don't change.)","✗ She eats very healthy. → ✓ She eats very healthily. (Describes the verb → adverb.)","✗ Exams are very stress. → ✓ Exams are very stressful. (Adjective → stressful.)"],"arabic":"الأفعال المركبة الصحية: cut down on (يقلّل من)، cut out (يتوقف تمامًا عن)، get over (يتعافى من)، come down with (يُصاب بمرض)، stay up (يسهر)، pass out (يُغمى عليه).\nالتعابير الاصطلاحية: under the weather (متوعّك قليلًا)، back on my feet (تعافيت)، take it easy (استرح ولا تُجهد نفسك)، burn the midnight oil (يسهر للدراسة أو العمل).\nعائلات الكلمات: health → healthy → healthily، stress → stressful."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Under the Weather, Back on My Feet: Health Phrasal Verbs, Idioms and Word Families”. Let’s learn health phrasal verbs (cut down on, cut out, get over, come down with, stay up, pass out); health idioms (under the weather, back on my feet, fit as a fiddle, take it easy, burn the midnight oil); health word families together.","on_screen":"GV-L06-U3-LS3 | Under the Weather, Back on My Feet: Health Phrasal Verbs, Idioms and Word Families","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Meet some new words. vitamin: a natural substance in food that keeps you healthy. posture: the way you hold your body when you sit or stand. mental: connected with the mind.","on_screen":"vitamin | posture | mental","visual":"Each word card flips over to show its picture (vocabulary image briefs) and Arabic meaning."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Phrasal verbs for health: cut down on (eat or use less), cut out (stop completely), get over (recover from), come down with (start to have an illness), stay up (not go to bed), pass out (become unconscious, faint). Idioms are phrases whose meaning is different from the words: under the weather = a little ill; back on my feet = healthy again; (as) fit as a fiddle = very healthy; take it easy = relax, don't work too hard; burn the midnight oil = study or work late at night.","on_screen":"health phrasal verbs (cut down on, cut out, get over, come down with, stay up, pass out); health idioms (under the weather, back on my feet, fit as a fiddle, take it easy, burn the midnight oil); health word families","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. I'm trying to cut down on sugar. My dad cut out fried food completely. It took me two weeks to get over the flu.","on_screen":"I'm trying to cut down on sugar. / My dad cut out fried food completely. / It took me two weeks to get over the flu.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I want to cut down sugar.” That’s not right. We say: “I want to cut down on sugar.” cut down on + noun.","on_screen":"✗ I want to cut down sugar.   ✓ I want to cut down on sugar.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"I'm under the weather.\" Am I very ill? … Think! … No – just a little ill. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"I came down with a cold, but I'm back on my feet now.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"I came down with a cold, but I'm back on my feet now.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: health phrasal verbs (cut down on, cut out, get over, come down with, stay up, pass out); health idioms (under the weather, back on my feet, fit as a fiddle, take it easy, burn the midnight oil); health word families.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","الأفعال المركبة الصحية: cut down on (يقلّل من)، cut out (يتوقف تمامًا عن)، get over (يتعافى من)، come down with (يُصاب بمرض)، stay up (يسهر)، pass out (يُغمى عليه).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I want to cut down sugar. — الصحيح: I want to cut down on sugar.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول I came down with a cold, but I'm back on my feet now."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"The doctor told my uncle to ___ salt. He uses too much.","options":["pass out","cut up","cut down on","come down with"],"answer":"cut down on","explanation":"Choose the right health phrasal verb.","explanation_ar":"الفعل المركب الصحيح."},{"q":"I ___ a fever last night, so I stayed home.","options":["came up with","came down with","got over","cut out"],"answer":"came down with","explanation":"Choose the right health phrasal verb.","explanation_ar":"الفعل المركب الصحيح."},{"q":"\"How are you?\" – \"A bit ___. I think I have a cold.\"","options":["over the moon","under the weather","fit as a fiddle","on cloud nine"],"answer":"under the weather","explanation":"Choose the idiom with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"التعبير الاصطلاحي."},{"q":"My grandmother is 80, but she's as fit as a ___!","options":["fiddle","feather","flower","fish"],"answer":"fiddle","explanation":"Choose the idiom with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"التعبير الاصطلاحي."},{"q":"Fruit and nuts are ___ snacks.","options":["nutrient it","nutritiously","nutritious","nutrition"],"answer":"nutritious","explanation":"Choose the right word-family form.","explanation_ar":"صيغة العائلة."},{"q":"Exams can be very ___.","options":["stressfully","stress","stressing it","stressful"],"answer":"stressful","explanation":"Choose the right word-family form.","explanation_ar":"صيغة العائلة."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS3-B1","type":"match","instructions":"Guided practice: Match the phrase to its meaning.","items":[{"q":"get over","options":["study or work late at night","healthy and active again","recover from an illness","suddenly become unconscious","relax and don't work too hard","not go to bed until late"],"answer":"recover from an illness","explanation":"get over → recover from an illness. Choose the right health phrasal verb.","explanation_ar":"الفعل المركب الصحيح."},{"q":"pass out","options":["study or work late at night","healthy and active again","recover from an illness","suddenly become unconscious","relax and don't work too hard","not go to bed until late"],"answer":"suddenly become unconscious","explanation":"pass out → suddenly become unconscious. Choose the right health phrasal verb.","explanation_ar":"الفعل المركب الصحيح."},{"q":"stay up","options":["study or work late at night","healthy and active again","recover from an illness","suddenly become unconscious","relax and don't work too hard","not go to bed until late"],"answer":"not go to bed until late","explanation":"stay up → not go to bed until late. Choose the right health phrasal verb.","explanation_ar":"الفعل المركب الصحيح."},{"q":"take it easy","options":["study or work late at night","healthy and active again","recover from an illness","suddenly become unconscious","relax and don't work too hard","not go to bed until late"],"answer":"relax and don't work too hard","explanation":"take it easy → relax and don't work too hard. Choose the right health phrasal verb.","explanation_ar":"الفعل المركب الصحيح."},{"q":"back on your feet","options":["study or work late at night","healthy and active again","recover from an illness","suddenly become unconscious","relax and don't work too hard","not go to bed until late"],"answer":"healthy and active again","explanation":"back on your feet → healthy and active again. Choose the right health phrasal verb.","explanation_ar":"الفعل المركب الصحيح."},{"q":"burn the midnight oil","options":["study or work late at night","healthy and active again","recover from an illness","suddenly become unconscious","relax and don't work too hard","not go to bed until late"],"answer":"study or work late at night","explanation":"burn the midnight oil → study or work late at night. Choose the right health phrasal verb.","explanation_ar":"الفعل المركب الصحيح."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS3-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Use the phrases.","items":[{"q":"Something you want to cut down on: ___","options":[],"answer":"I want to cut down on chips.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses health phrasal verbs (cut down on, cut out, get over, come down with, stay up, pass out); health idioms (under the weather, back on my feet, fit as a fiddle, take it easy, burn the midnight oil); health word families correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"The last time you came down with something: ___","options":[],"answer":"I came down with a cold last winter.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses health phrasal verbs (cut down on, cut out, get over, come down with, stay up, pass out); health idioms (under the weather, back on my feet, fit as a fiddle, take it easy, burn the midnight oil); health word families correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"How long it took you to get over an illness: ___","options":[],"answer":"It took me five days to get over the flu.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses health phrasal verbs (cut down on, cut out, get over, come down with, stay up, pass out); health idioms (under the weather, back on my feet, fit as a fiddle, take it easy, burn the midnight oil); health word families correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"When do you burn the midnight oil?","options":[],"answer":"I burn the midnight oil before final exams.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses health phrasal verbs (cut down on, cut out, get over, come down with, stay up, pass out); health idioms (under the weather, back on my feet, fit as a fiddle, take it easy, burn the midnight oil); health word families correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence with \"healthily\".","options":[],"answer":"My grandparents eat healthily and walk every day.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses health phrasal verbs (cut down on, cut out, get over, come down with, stay up, pass out); health idioms (under the weather, back on my feet, fit as a fiddle, take it easy, burn the midnight oil); health word families correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS3-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Get well soon.","items":[{"q":"Write a get-well message to a friend using 2 idioms.","options":[],"answer":"Sorry you're under the weather! Take it easy, and I hope you're back on your feet soon.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses health phrasal verbs (cut down on, cut out, get over, come down with, stay up, pass out); health idioms (under the weather, back on my feet, fit as a fiddle, take it easy, burn the midnight oil); health word families correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences about a healthier lifestyle with cut down on and cut out.","options":[],"answer":"I'm going to cut down on sweets. My brother has cut out energy drinks.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses health phrasal verbs (cut down on, cut out, get over, come down with, stay up, pass out); health idioms (under the weather, back on my feet, fit as a fiddle, take it easy, burn the midnight oil); health word families correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences with word-family forms (energetic, relaxation, recovery…).","options":[],"answer":"A good breakfast makes me energetic. Reading is my favorite form of relaxation.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses health phrasal verbs (cut down on, cut out, get over, come down with, stay up, pass out); health idioms (under the weather, back on my feet, fit as a fiddle, take it easy, burn the midnight oil); health word families correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Word Family Tree","mechanic":"drag_and_drop","rules":["Teams take turns drawing a word card.","Place the card on the correct branch of the tree and say a sentence with it.","Correct placement and sentence = 2 points.","The team with the most points when the tree is full wins."],"data":[{"word":"healthy","category":"adjective","family":"health"},{"word":"healthily","category":"adverb","family":"health"},{"word":"stressful","category":"adjective","family":"stress"},{"word":"stressed","category":"adjective","family":"stress"},{"word":"energetic","category":"adjective","family":"energy"},{"word":"energize","category":"verb","family":"energy"},{"word":"recovery","category":"noun","family":"recover"},{"word":"relaxation","category":"noun","family":"relax"},{"word":"relaxed","category":"adjective","family":"relax"},{"word":"nutritious","category":"adjective","family":"nutrition"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"My father ___ sugar from his tea completely.","options":["cut down","passed out","came down with","cut out"],"answer":"cut out","explanation":"Choose the right health phrasal verb.","explanation_ar":"الفعل المركب الصحيح."},{"q":"It was so hot that one of the runners ___.","options":["cut out","passed out","got over","passed by"],"answer":"passed out","explanation":"Choose the right health phrasal verb.","explanation_ar":"الفعل المركب الصحيح."},{"q":"Don't ___ late – you have a test tomorrow!","options":["stay out of","get over","stay up","cut out"],"answer":"stay up","explanation":"Choose the right health phrasal verb.","explanation_ar":"الفعل المركب الصحيح."},{"q":"You've worked all day. ___ this evening.","options":["Do it easy","Take it hard","Make it easy","Take it easy"],"answer":"Take it easy","explanation":"Choose the idiom with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"التعبير الاصطلاحي."},{"q":"I was ill last week, but now I'm ___.","options":["under the weather","back on my feet","burning the midnight oil","up in the air"],"answer":"back on my feet","explanation":"Choose the idiom with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"التعبير الاصطلاحي."},{"q":"Before the exam, Noura was ___ – she studied until 2 a.m.","options":["taking it easy","fit as a fiddle","under the weather","burning the midnight oil"],"answer":"burning the midnight oil","explanation":"Choose the idiom with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"التعبير الاصطلاحي."},{"q":"The doctor said my ___ will take a month.","options":["recovery","recover","recovered","recovering it"],"answer":"recovery","explanation":"Choose the right word-family form.","explanation_ar":"صيغة العائلة."},{"q":"After the holiday, I felt ___ and full of energy.","options":["relaxed","relaxing it","relax","relaxation"],"answer":"relaxed","explanation":"Choose the right word-family form.","explanation_ar":"صيغة العائلة."},{"q":"","options":["My grandparents eat healthful.","My grandparents eat health.","My grandparents eat healthily.","My grandparents eat healthy-ly."],"answer":"My grandparents eat healthily.","explanation":"Choose the right word-family form.","explanation_ar":"صيغة العائلة."},{"q":"A sign of an illness is called a ___.","options":["habit","vitamin","symptom","posture"],"answer":"symptom","explanation":"Choose the health word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى الصحيح."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS3-IMG01","prompt":"A comic strip in four panels: Adam feeling \"under the weather\" in bed with a thermometer; his mother telling him to \"take it easy\"; Adam \"cutting down on\" sweets; Adam \"back on his feet\", fit as a fiddle, playing football. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A comic strip in four panels: Adam feeling \"under the weather\" in bed with a thermometer; his mother telling him to \"take it easy\"; Adam \"cutting down on\" sweets; Adam \"back on his feet\", fit as a fiddle, playing football"},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS3-IMG02","prompt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 6 small picture icons of the lesson words; empty labels. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 6 small picture icons of the lesson words"},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS3-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows vitamin (a natural substance in food that keeps you healthy); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing vitamin: a natural substance in food that keeps you healthy"},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS3-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows posture (the way you hold your body when you sit or stand); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing posture: the way you hold your body when you sit or stand"},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS3-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows mental (connected with the mind); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing mental: connected with the mind"},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS3-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows symptom (a sign of an illness); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing symptom: a sign of an illness"},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS3-W05","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows recover (to get better after an illness); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing recover: to get better after an illness"},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS3-W06","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows energetic (full of energy); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing energetic: full of energy"},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS3-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Word Family Tree”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Word Family Tree"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U3-LS3-W01","script":"vitamin. vitamin. Oranges contain vitamin C.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U3-LS3-W02","script":"posture. posture. Bad posture can hurt your back.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U3-LS3-W03","script":"mental. mental. Mental health is as important as physical health.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U3-LS3-W04","script":"symptom. symptom. A high temperature is a symptom of the flu.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U3-LS3-W05","script":"recover. recover. It took me a week to recover from the flu.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U3-LS3-W06","script":"energetic. energetic. I feel energetic after a good breakfast.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U3-LS3-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Under the Weather, Back on My Feet: Health Phrasal Verbs, Idioms and Word Families”. Let’s learn health phrasal verbs (cut down on, cut out, get over, come down with, stay up, pass out); health idioms (under the weather, back on my feet, fit as a fiddle, take it easy, burn the midnight oil); health word families together. Meet some new words. vitamin: a natural substance in food that keeps you healthy. posture: the way you hold your body when you sit or stand. mental: connected with the mind. Phrasal verbs for health: cut down on (eat or use less), cut out (stop completely), get over (recover from), come down with (start to have an illness), stay up (not go to bed), pass out (become unconscious, faint). Idioms are phrases whose meaning is different from the words: under the weather = a little ill; back on my feet = healthy again; (as) fit as a fiddle = very healthy; take it easy = relax, don't work too hard; burn the midnight oil = study or work late at night. Here are some examples. I'm trying to cut down on sugar. My dad cut out fried food completely. It took me two weeks to get over the flu. Be careful! Some learners say: “I want to cut down sugar.” That’s not right. We say: “I want to cut down on sugar.” cut down on + noun. Quick check: \"I'm under the weather.\" Am I very ill? … Think! … No – just a little ill. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"I came down with a cold, but I'm back on my feet now.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.95"}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS4","title":"Necessary, Definitely, Separate: Commonly Misspelled Words","objectives":["Students will be able to spell commonly misspelled words correctly.","Students will be able to apply spelling rules for ie/ei, doubling consonants and silent letters.","I can spell words like \"necessary\", \"definitely\" and \"receive\".","I can find and fix spelling mistakes in a text."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من تهجئة الكلمات التي يكثر الخطأ فيها بشكل صحيح.","سيتمكن الطلاب من تطبيق قواعد التهجئة الخاصة بـ ie/ei ومضاعفة الحروف الساكنة والحروف الصامتة.","أستطيع أن أتهجّى كلمات مثل necessary وdefinitely وreceive.","أستطيع أن أجد أخطاء التهجئة في النص وأصححها."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"nutrition","pos":"noun","ipa":"/nuˈtrɪʃən/","definition":"the food your body needs to grow and stay healthy","arabic":"التغذية","example":"Good nutrition helps you concentrate in class.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"balanced","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈbælənst/","definition":"with the right amounts of different things","arabic":"متوازن","example":"A balanced diet includes fruit, vegetables and protein.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"habit","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈhæbət/","definition":"something you do often, usually without thinking","arabic":"عادة","example":"Brushing your teeth twice a day is a good habit.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"stress","pos":"noun","ipa":"/strɛs/","definition":"a feeling of worry because of problems or pressure","arabic":"توتّر / ضغط نفسي","example":"Exams can cause stress.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"exercise","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɛksɚˌsaɪz/","definition":"physical activity to stay fit and healthy","arabic":"تمارين رياضية","example":"Thirty minutes of exercise a day is enough for most people.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"hydrated","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈhaɪˌdreɪtəd/","definition":"having enough water in your body","arabic":"مرتوٍ (جسمه فيه ماء كافٍ)","example":"Stay hydrated in the summer heat.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"i before e, except after c (when it sounds like \"ee\"): believe, achieve, piece – but receive, ceiling. Learn the exceptions: weird, seize, protein.\nDouble the final consonant when a short word (or a stressed last syllable) ends in consonant + vowel + consonant and you add -ing / -ed: stop → stopping, begin → beginning, prefer → preferred. But: visit → visiting (stress on the first syllable).\nWatch for silent letters (muscle, stomach, wrist, knee, hour) and double letters: necessary (one c, two s), accommodation, recommend (one c, two m), occasionally, definitely (not \"definately\"). Words ending in -ful have one l, but -fully has two: careful → carefully.\ni before e except after c: believe ↔ receive\nstop → stopping • begin → beginning • visit → visiting\nsilent letters: muscle, stomach, knee, wrist, hour\none c two s: necessary • one c two m: recommend","examples":["I believe in healthy eating.","Did you receive my message?","Exercise is necessary for good health.","I definitely feel better after a walk.","Keep raw meat separate from vegetables.","At the beginning of the year, I started swimming.","Stretching helps your muscles.","The doctor recommended more sleep."],"common_errors":["✗ I recieved a medal. → ✓ I received a medal. (After c → ei.)","✗ Sleep is very neccesary. → ✓ Sleep is very necessary. (One c, two s.)","✗ I will definately come. → ✓ I will definitely come. (defin-ite-ly.)","✗ We are begining a new diet. → ✓ We are beginning a new diet. (Double n.)"],"arabic":"قاعدة i قبل e إلا بعد c: believe لكن receive.\nنضاعف الحرف الأخير عند إضافة ing أو ed في الكلمات القصيرة التي تنتهي بساكن + متحرك + ساكن: stop → stopping، begin → beginning.\nانتبه للحروف الصامتة: muscle وstomach وknee.\nnecessary فيها c واحدة وs مضاعفة، وrecommend فيها c واحدة وm مضاعفة."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Necessary, Definitely, Separate: Commonly Misspelled Words”. Let’s learn spelling rules and commonly misspelled words: i before e (except after c), doubling the final consonant (begin → beginning), silent letters (muscle, stomach), -ful / -fully, double letters (necessary, recommend, occasionally) together.","on_screen":"GV-L06-U3-LS4 | Necessary, Definitely, Separate: Commonly Misspelled Words","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"i before e, except after c (when it sounds like \"ee\"): believe, achieve, piece – but receive, ceiling. Learn the exceptions: weird, seize, protein.","on_screen":"spelling rules and commonly misspelled words: i before e (except after c), doubling the final consonant (begin → beginning), silent letters (muscle, stomach), -ful / -fully, double letters (necessary, recommend, occasionally)","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"i before e, except after c (when it sounds like \"ee\"): believe, achieve, piece – but receive, ceiling. Learn the exceptions: weird, seize, protein. Double the final consonant when a short word (or a stressed last syllable) ends in consonant + vowel + consonant and you add -ing / -ed: stop → stopping, begin → beginning, prefer → preferred. But: visit → visiting (stress on the first syllable).","on_screen":"i before e except after c: believe ↔ receive • stop → stopping • begin → beginning • visit → visiting • silent letters: muscle, stomach, knee, wrist, hour","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. I believe in healthy eating. Did you receive my message? Exercise is necessary for good health.","on_screen":"I believe in healthy eating. / Did you receive my message? / Exercise is necessary for good health.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I recieved a medal.” That’s not right. We say: “I received a medal.” After c → ei.","on_screen":"✗ I recieved a medal.   ✓ I received a medal.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"recieve\" or \"receive\"? … Think! … *receive* – after c, e comes before i. Great job! Now you can say: I can spell words like \"necessary\", \"definitely\" and \"receive\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can spell words like \"necessary\", \"definitely\" and \"receive\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: spelling rules and commonly misspelled words: i before e (except after c), doubling the final consonant (begin → beginning), silent letters (muscle, stomach), -ful / -fully, double letters (necessary, recommend, occasionally).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","قاعدة i قبل e إلا بعد c: believe لكن receive.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I recieved a medal. — الصحيح: I received a medal.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أتهجّى كلمات مثل necessary وdefinitely وreceive."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"My Fitness Journey (editing passage)","body":"At the begining of the year, I made a decision. I definately wanted to get fit. My coach recomended swimming, so I started swiming three times a week. It's neccessary to drink water, so I carry a bottle. My mussles are stronger now, and last month I recieved a certificate!","word_count":50,"audio_id":""}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct spelling.","items":[{"q":"","options":["recieve","resieve","receeve","receive"],"answer":"receive","explanation":"i before e, except after c.","explanation_ar":"قاعدة ie."},{"q":"","options":["necessary","neccesary","necesary","neccessary"],"answer":"necessary","explanation":"Double or single letters (necessary, recommend, occasionally).","explanation_ar":"الحروف المضاعفة."},{"q":"","options":["definitly","definitely","defenitely","definately"],"answer":"definitely","explanation":"Commonly misspelled word.","explanation_ar":"كلمة شائعة الخطأ."},{"q":"","options":["beggining","begining","beginning","beginnig"],"answer":"beginning","explanation":"Double the final consonant (stopping, beginning).","explanation_ar":"مضاعفة الحرف."},{"q":"","options":["musle","muscle","muscel","mussle"],"answer":"muscle","explanation":"Silent letters (muscle, stomach, knee).","explanation_ar":"الحروف الصامتة."},{"q":"","options":["seprate","seperate","separete","separate"],"answer":"separate","explanation":"Commonly misspelled word.","explanation_ar":"كلمة شائعة الخطأ."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS4-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the spelling.","items":[{"q":"My grandmother doesn't beleive in fast food.","options":[],"answer":"My grandmother doesn't believe in fast food.","explanation":"beleive → believe. i before e, except after c.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: beleive → believe. قاعدة ie."},{"q":"The doctor recomended a balanced diet.","options":[],"answer":"The doctor recommended a balanced diet.","explanation":"recomended → recommended. Double or single letters (necessary, recommend, occasionally).","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: recomended → recommended. الحروف المضاعفة."},{"q":"I have a pain in my stomack.","options":[],"answer":"I have a pain in my stomach.","explanation":"stomack → stomach. Silent letters (muscle, stomach, knee).","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: stomack → stomach. الحروف الصامتة."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS4-B2","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Write the -ing form. Word bank: planning, jogging, visiting","items":[{"q":"Write the -ing form of jog: ______","options":[],"answer":"jogging","explanation":"Double the final consonant (stopping, beginning).","explanation_ar":"مضاعفة الحرف."},{"q":"Write the -ing form of visit: ______","options":[],"answer":"visiting","explanation":"Double the final consonant (stopping, beginning).","explanation_ar":"مضاعفة الحرف."},{"q":"Write the -ing form of plan: ______","options":[],"answer":"planning","explanation":"Double the final consonant (stopping, beginning).","explanation_ar":"مضاعفة الحرف."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS4-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Edit the health blog.","items":[{"q":"At the begining of the year, I made a decision.","options":[],"answer":"At the beginning of the year, I made a decision.","explanation":"begining → beginning. i before e, except after c.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: begining → beginning. قاعدة ie."},{"q":"I definately wanted to get fit.","options":[],"answer":"I definitely wanted to get fit.","explanation":"definately → definitely. i before e, except after c.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: definately → definitely. قاعدة ie."},{"q":"My coach recomended swimming, so I started swimming three times a week.","options":[],"answer":"My coach recommended swimming, so I started swimming three times a week.","explanation":"recomended → recommended. i before e, except after c.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: recomended → recommended. قاعدة ie."},{"q":"My coach recommended swimming, so I started swiming three times a week.","options":[],"answer":"My coach recommended swimming, so I started swimming three times a week.","explanation":"swiming → swimming. i before e, except after c.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: swiming → swimming. قاعدة ie."},{"q":"It's neccessary to drink water, so I carry a bottle.","options":[],"answer":"It's necessary to drink water, so I carry a bottle.","explanation":"neccessary → necessary. i before e, except after c.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: neccessary → necessary. قاعدة ie."},{"q":"My mussles are stronger now, and last month I received a certificate!","options":[],"answer":"My muscles are stronger now, and last month I received a certificate!","explanation":"mussles → muscles. i before e, except after c.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: mussles → muscles. قاعدة ie."},{"q":"My muscles are stronger now, and last month I recieved a certificate!","options":[],"answer":"My muscles are stronger now, and last month I received a certificate!","explanation":"recieved → received. i before e, except after c.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: recieved → received. قاعدة ie."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS4-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Your spelling list.","items":[{"q":"Write 3 words you often misspell and a tip to remember each.","options":[],"answer":"necessary – one collar, two sleeves (1 c, 2 s); definitely – there's \"finite\" inside; separate – there's \"a rat\" in it.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses spelling rules and commonly misspelled words: i before e (except after c), doubling the final consonant (begin → beginning), silent letters (muscle, stomach), -ful / -fully, double letters (necessary, recommend, occasionally) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences with \"necessary\" and \"recommend\".","options":[],"answer":"It's necessary to warm up before a match. I recommend this healthy café.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses spelling rules and commonly misspelled words: i before e (except after c), doubling the final consonant (begin → beginning), silent letters (muscle, stomach), -ful / -fully, double letters (necessary, recommend, occasionally) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence with a word that has a silent letter.","options":[],"answer":"I hurt my knee playing football.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses spelling rules and commonly misspelled words: i before e (except after c), doubling the final consonant (begin → beginning), silent letters (muscle, stomach), -ful / -fully, double letters (necessary, recommend, occasionally) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Spelling Relay","mechanic":"word_builder","rules":["Teams line up facing the board.","The teacher says a word; the first student runs to the board and writes the first letter.","The next student adds the next letter, and so on.","The first team with the correct spelling wins the point."],"data":[{"word":"necessary","clue":""},{"word":"definitely","clue":""},{"word":"separate","clue":""},{"word":"receive","clue":""},{"word":"beginning","clue":""},{"word":"muscle","clue":""},{"word":"nutrition","clue":"the food your body needs to grow and stay healthy"},{"word":"balanced","clue":"with the right amounts of different things"},{"word":"habit","clue":"something you do often, usually without thinking"},{"word":"stress","clue":"a feeling of worry because of problems or pressure"},{"word":"exercise","clue":"physical activity to stay fit and healthy"},{"word":"hydrated","clue":"having enough water in your body"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"","options":["achieve","acheeve","acheive","achive"],"answer":"achieve","explanation":"i before e, except after c.","explanation_ar":"قاعدة ie."},{"q":"","options":["occassionally","ocasionally","occasionally","ocassionaly"],"answer":"occasionally","explanation":"Double or single letters (necessary, recommend, occasionally).","explanation_ar":"الحروف المضاعفة."},{"q":"","options":["stomach","stomak","stummach","stomack"],"answer":"stomach","explanation":"Silent letters (muscle, stomach, knee).","explanation_ar":"الحروف الصامتة."},{"q":"","options":["stoped","stopped","stopt","stoppd"],"answer":"stopped","explanation":"Double the final consonant (stopping, beginning).","explanation_ar":"مضاعفة الحرف."},{"q":"","options":["carefuly","carefuley","carefully","carfully"],"answer":"carefully","explanation":"Double or single letters (necessary, recommend, occasionally).","explanation_ar":"الحروف المضاعفة."},{"q":"Which word has a silent letter?","options":["arm","knee","hand","leg"],"answer":"knee","explanation":"Silent letters (muscle, stomach, knee).","explanation_ar":"الحروف الصامتة."},{"q":"","options":["recommend","recomend","reccomend","reccommend"],"answer":"recommend","explanation":"Double or single letters (necessary, recommend, occasionally).","explanation_ar":"الحروف المضاعفة."},{"q":"","options":["sealing","cieling","ceeling","ceiling"],"answer":"ceiling","explanation":"i before e, except after c.","explanation_ar":"قاعدة ie."},{"q":"","options":["prefered","prefferred","preferd","preferred"],"answer":"preferred","explanation":"Double the final consonant (stopping, beginning).","explanation_ar":"مضاعفة الحرف."},{"q":"","options":["exercize","excercise","exercise","exersize"],"answer":"exercise","explanation":"Commonly misspelled word.","explanation_ar":"كلمة شائعة الخطأ."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS4-IMG01","prompt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Healthy Body, Healthy Mind” that shows spelling rules and commonly misspelled words: i before e (except after c), doubling the final consonant (begin → beginning), silent letters (muscle, stomach), -ful / -fully, double letters (necessary, recommend, occasionally) in action. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Healthy Body, Healthy Mind” that shows spelling rules and commonly misspelled words: i before e (except after c), doubling the final consonant (begin → beginning), silent letters (muscle, stomach), -ful / -fully, double letters (necessary, recommend, occasionally) in action"},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS4-IMG02","prompt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen"},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS4-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Spelling Relay”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Spelling Relay"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U3-LS4-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Necessary, Definitely, Separate: Commonly Misspelled Words”. Let’s learn spelling rules and commonly misspelled words: i before e (except after c), doubling the final consonant (begin → beginning), silent letters (muscle, stomach), -ful / -fully, double letters (necessary, recommend, occasionally) together. i before e, except after c (when it sounds like \"ee\"): believe, achieve, piece – but receive, ceiling. Learn the exceptions: weird, seize, protein. i before e, except after c (when it sounds like \"ee\"): believe, achieve, piece – but receive, ceiling. Learn the exceptions: weird, seize, protein. Double the final consonant when a short word (or a stressed last syllable) ends in consonant + vowel + consonant and you add -ing / -ed: stop → stopping, begin → beginning, prefer → preferred. But: visit → visiting (stress on the first syllable). Here are some examples. I believe in healthy eating. Did you receive my message? Exercise is necessary for good health. Be careful! Some learners say: “I recieved a medal.” That’s not right. We say: “I received a medal.” After c → ei. Quick check: \"recieve\" or \"receive\"? … Think! … *receive* – after c, e comes before i. Great job! Now you can say: I can spell words like \"necessary\", \"definitely\" and \"receive\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.95"}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS5","title":"Healthy Body, Healthy Mind: Our Class Leaflet – Language in Use","objectives":["Students will be able to give and discuss advice about healthy habits.","Students will be able to write a health leaflet with gerunds, infinitives and correct spelling.","I can give health advice to my classmates.","I can write a health leaflet with no spelling mistakes."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من تقديم النصائح حول العادات الصحية ومناقشتها.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة نشرة صحية بصيغ ing وto وبتهجئة صحيحة.","أستطيع أن أقدّم نصائح صحية لزملائي.","أستطيع أن أكتب نشرة صحية خالية من الأخطاء الإملائية."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"nutrition","pos":"noun","ipa":"/nuˈtrɪʃən/","definition":"the food your body needs to grow and stay healthy","arabic":"التغذية","example":"Good nutrition helps you concentrate in class.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"balanced","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈbælənst/","definition":"with the right amounts of different things","arabic":"متوازن","example":"A balanced diet includes fruit, vegetables and protein.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"habit","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈhæbət/","definition":"something you do often, usually without thinking","arabic":"عادة","example":"Brushing your teeth twice a day is a good habit.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"stress","pos":"noun","ipa":"/strɛs/","definition":"a feeling of worry because of problems or pressure","arabic":"توتّر / ضغط نفسي","example":"Exams can cause stress.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"exercise","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɛksɚˌsaɪz/","definition":"physical activity to stay fit and healthy","arabic":"تمارين رياضية","example":"Thirty minutes of exercise a day is enough for most people.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"hydrated","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈhaɪˌdreɪtəd/","definition":"having enough water in your body","arabic":"مرتوٍ (جسمه فيه ماء كافٍ)","example":"Stay hydrated in the summer heat.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"immune system","pos":"noun phrase","ipa":"/ˌɪˈmjun ˈsɪstəm/","definition":"the parts of the body that fight illness","arabic":"جهاز المناعة","example":"Sleep helps your immune system.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"protein","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈproʊˌtin/","definition":"a substance in food like meat, eggs and beans that builds muscles","arabic":"بروتين","example":"Eggs are full of protein.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"vitamin","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈvaɪtəmən/","definition":"a natural substance in food that keeps you healthy","arabic":"فيتامين","example":"Oranges contain vitamin C.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"posture","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈpɑstʃɚ/","definition":"the way you hold your body when you sit or stand","arabic":"وضعية الجسم","example":"Bad posture can hurt your back.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"mental","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈmɛntəl/","definition":"connected with the mind","arabic":"ذهني / نفسي","example":"Mental health is as important as physical health.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"symptom","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈsɪmptəm/","definition":"a sign of an illness","arabic":"عَرَض (للمرض)","example":"A high temperature is a symptom of the flu.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"recover","pos":"verb","ipa":"/rɪˈkʌvɚ/","definition":"to get better after an illness","arabic":"يتعافى","example":"It took me a week to recover from the flu.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"energetic","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˌɛnɚˈdʒɛtɪk/","definition":"full of energy","arabic":"نشيط / مفعم بالحيوية","example":"I feel energetic after a good breakfast.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Today you use all of Unit 3: gerunds and infinitives, -ing subjects, preposition + -ing, health phrasal verbs and idioms, word families and spelling.\nA health leaflet gives clear advice (try to…, avoid…, it's necessary to…), explains why (Staying hydrated helps…) and ends with encouragement.\n✔ enjoy / avoid / keep + -ing • decide / try / hope + to\n✔ -ing subject + singular verb • preposition + -ing\n✔ cut down on • get over • under the weather • take it easy\n✔ necessary, definitely, recommend, receive, separate","examples":["Eating slowly helps your stomach.","Try to stand up every hour.","Avoid drinking energy drinks.","I'm looking forward to joining the walking club.","Cut down on fried food.","Remember to stretch your muscles.","It's necessary to wash fruit before eating it.","Good posture protects your back."],"common_errors":["✗ Avoid to drink soda. → ✓ Avoid drinking soda. (avoid + -ing.)","✗ Sleep early help you grow. → ✓ Sleeping early helps you grow. (-ing subject + singular verb.)","✗ Exercise is neccessary. → ✓ Exercise is necessary. (Spelling: one c, two s.)"],"arabic":"نراجع صيغ ing وto، وing فاعلًا وبعد حروف الجر، والأفعال المركبة والتعابير الصحية والتهجئة.\nالنشرة الصحية تقدّم نصائح واضحة، وتشرح السبب، وتنتهي بالتشجيع.\nتذكّر: avoid + ing، وdecide + to، والفعل بعد فاعل ing مفرد."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Healthy Body, Healthy Mind: Our Class Leaflet – Language in Use”. Let’s learn gerunds and infinitives, -ing subjects and preposition + -ing, health phrasal verbs, idioms and word families, commonly misspelled words (unit review) together.","on_screen":"GV-L06-U3-LS5 | Healthy Body, Healthy Mind: Our Class Leaflet – Language in Use","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Health talk show: in pairs, one student is a health expert, the other is a TV presenter. The presenter asks 5 questions (What do you suggest doing…? What should teenagers avoid…?). The expert answers with gerunds, infinitives, a phrasal verb and an idiom.","on_screen":"Language in use","visual":"Split screen: two cast members talking, with speech bubbles appearing."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Today you use all of Unit 3: gerunds and infinitives, -ing subjects, preposition + -ing, health phrasal verbs and idioms, word families and spelling. A health leaflet gives clear advice (try to…, avoid…, it's necessary to…), explains why (Staying hydrated helps…) and ends with encouragement.","on_screen":"✔ enjoy / avoid / keep + -ing • decide / try / hope + to • ✔ -ing subject + singular verb • preposition + -ing • ✔ cut down on • get over • under the weather • take it easy","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Eating slowly helps your stomach. Try to stand up every hour. Avoid drinking energy drinks.","on_screen":"Eating slowly helps your stomach. / Try to stand up every hour. / Avoid drinking energy drinks.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “Avoid to drink soda.” That’s not right. We say: “Avoid drinking soda.” avoid + -ing.","on_screen":"✗ Avoid to drink soda.   ✓ Avoid drinking soda.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: what is wrong with “Sleep early help you grow.”? … Think! … It should be “Sleeping early helps you grow.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can give health advice to my classmates.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can give health advice to my classmates.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: gerunds and infinitives, -ing subjects and preposition + -ing, health phrasal verbs, idioms and word families, commonly misspelled words (unit review).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نراجع صيغ ing وto، وing فاعلًا وبعد حروف الجر، والأفعال المركبة والتعابير الصحية والتهجئة.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: Avoid to drink soda. — الصحيح: Avoid drinking soda.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقدّم نصائح صحية لزملائي."]},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"Healthy Body, Healthy Mind – Grade 8 Leaflet","body":"Taking care of your body and mind is easier than you think!\nFirst, try to drink at least six glasses of water a day. Staying hydrated helps you concentrate.\nAvoid skipping breakfast – a balanced meal gives you energy for the whole morning.\nIf you enjoy playing sports, keep doing it! If not, start walking for twenty minutes after school.\nIt's also necessary to cut down on screen time before bed. Instead of scrolling on your phone, read a book.\nWhen you feel stressed, talk to someone you trust. Remember: everyone feels under the weather sometimes.\nWe definitely recommend sleeping eight to nine hours a night. You'll feel energetic and fit as a fiddle!","word_count":114,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U3-LS5-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS5-A1","type":"true_false","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read the leaflet. True or False?","items":[{"q":"The leaflet says you should drink at least six glasses of water a day.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Healthy Body, Healthy Mind – Grade 8 Leaflet”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"It says skipping breakfast is a good idea.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Healthy Body, Healthy Mind – Grade 8 Leaflet”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"If you don't play sports, it suggests walking for twenty minutes after school.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Healthy Body, Healthy Mind – Grade 8 Leaflet”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"It recommends using your phone before bed.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Healthy Body, Healthy Mind – Grade 8 Leaflet”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"It says everyone feels a little ill sometimes.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Healthy Body, Healthy Mind – Grade 8 Leaflet”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"It recommends sleeping five hours a night.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Healthy Body, Healthy Mind – Grade 8 Leaflet”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS5-B1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Guided practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"Try ___ at least six glasses of water a day.","options":["to drink","drink","drinking at","drank"],"answer":"to drink","explanation":"Gerund or infinitive after a verb.","explanation_ar":"ing أم to بعد الفعل."},{"q":"Avoid ___ breakfast.","options":["to skip","skipped","skipping","skip"],"answer":"skipping","explanation":"Gerund or infinitive after a verb.","explanation_ar":"ing أم to بعد الفعل."},{"q":"___ hydrated helps you concentrate.","options":["Stay","Staying","To staying","Stays"],"answer":"Staying","explanation":"-ing subject / preposition + -ing.","explanation_ar":"ing فاعلًا أو بعد حرف جر."},{"q":"Instead of ___ on your phone, read a book.","options":["scrolling","scroll","scrolled","to scroll"],"answer":"scrolling","explanation":"-ing subject / preposition + -ing.","explanation_ar":"ing فاعلًا أو بعد حرف جر."},{"q":"It's necessary to ___ screen time before bed.","options":["come down with","cut out of","pass out","cut down on"],"answer":"cut down on","explanation":"Health phrasal verb, idiom or word family.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال المركبة والتعابير."},{"q":"","options":["We definately recommend sleeping eight hours.","We definitely recommend sleeping eight hours.","We definitly reccommend sleeping eight hours.","We definitely recomend sleeping eight hours."],"answer":"We definitely recommend sleeping eight hours.","explanation":"Correct spelling.","explanation_ar":"التهجئة الصحيحة."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS5-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Prepare your health talk show.","items":[{"q":"Presenter question 1 (What do you suggest…?): ___","options":[],"answer":"What do you suggest doing when you feel stressed?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses gerunds and infinitives, -ing subjects and preposition + -ing, health phrasal verbs, idioms and word families, commonly misspelled words (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Expert answer with suggest / recommend + -ing: ___","options":[],"answer":"I recommend going for a walk or talking to a friend.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses gerunds and infinitives, -ing subjects and preposition + -ing, health phrasal verbs, idioms and word families, commonly misspelled words (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Presenter question 2 (What should teenagers avoid…?): ___","options":[],"answer":"What should teenagers avoid doing before bed?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses gerunds and infinitives, -ing subjects and preposition + -ing, health phrasal verbs, idioms and word families, commonly misspelled words (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Expert answer with avoid + -ing: ___","options":[],"answer":"They should avoid using screens for an hour before bed.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses gerunds and infinitives, -ing subjects and preposition + -ing, health phrasal verbs, idioms and word families, commonly misspelled words (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Expert's final tip with an idiom: ___","options":[],"answer":"If you feel under the weather, take it easy and rest.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses gerunds and infinitives, -ing subjects and preposition + -ing, health phrasal verbs, idioms and word families, commonly misspelled words (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS5-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write your health leaflet.","items":[{"q":"Plan: title, 2 -ing subjects, 2 verb + -ing, 2 verb + to, 1 preposition + -ing, 1 phrasal verb/idiom, 3 spelling-list words.","options":[],"answer":"Title: Fit for School!; Eating fruit…, Sleeping early…; enjoy walking, avoid drinking; try to stretch, remember to drink; before running; cut down on sugar; necessary, recommend, muscles","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses gerunds and infinitives, -ing subjects and preposition + -ing, health phrasal verbs, idioms and word families, commonly misspelled words (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write your leaflet in 7–8 sentences.","options":[],"answer":"Fit for School! Eating fruit every day keeps your immune system strong. Sleeping early helps you concentrate in class. If you enjoy walking, walk to school with a friend. Avoid drinking sugary drinks. Try to stretch your muscles before running. Remember to drink water at break time. It's necessary to cut down on sugar. We recommend taking it easy on weekends too!","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses gerunds and infinitives, -ing subjects and preposition + -ing, health phrasal verbs, idioms and word families, commonly misspelled words (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Check: -ing or to? singular verb after -ing? spelling? Fix one mistake.","options":[],"answer":"I changed \"Avoid to drink\" to \"Avoid drinking\" and \"neccessary\" to \"necessary\".","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses gerunds and infinitives, -ing subjects and preposition + -ing, health phrasal verbs, idioms and word families, commonly misspelled words (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Board Race Review","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["One student from each team stands at the board.","The teacher says a cue word and a task (meaning, spelling or sentence with gerunds and infinitives, -ing subjects and preposition + -ing, health phrasal verbs, idioms and word families, commonly misspelled words (unit review)).","The first correct answer wins a point; rotate players every round.","Play 10 rounds."],"data":[{"cue":"nutrition","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"balanced","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"habit","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"stress","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"exercise","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"hydrated","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"immune system","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"protein","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"vitamin","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"posture","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"mental","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"symptom","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"recover","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"energetic","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"I've decided ___ a vegetable garden at home.","options":["to starting","to start","starting","start"],"answer":"to start","explanation":"Gerund or infinitive after a verb.","explanation_ar":"ing أم to بعد الفعل."},{"q":"Do you enjoy ___ healthy meals?","options":["cooked","to cook","cook","cooking"],"answer":"cooking","explanation":"Gerund or infinitive after a verb.","explanation_ar":"ing أم to بعد الفعل."},{"q":"","options":["To walking to school is good exercise.","Walking to school is good exercise.","Walking to school are good exercise.","Walk to school is good exercise."],"answer":"Walking to school is good exercise.","explanation":"-ing subject / preposition + -ing.","explanation_ar":"ing فاعلًا أو بعد حرف جر."},{"q":"She's good at ___ people feel better.","options":["make","making","to make","made"],"answer":"making","explanation":"-ing subject / preposition + -ing.","explanation_ar":"ing فاعلًا أو بعد حرف جر."},{"q":"I've finally ___ my cold. I feel great!","options":["cut out","came down with","got over","got on"],"answer":"got over","explanation":"Health phrasal verb, idiom or word family.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال المركبة والتعابير."},{"q":"I'm a bit ___ today. I think I'll stay home.","options":["under the weather","over the moon","fit as a fiddle","back on my feet"],"answer":"under the weather","explanation":"Health phrasal verb, idiom or word family.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال المركبة والتعابير."},{"q":"Eating ___ helps you stay energetic.","options":["healthily","healthy","healthier it","health"],"answer":"healthily","explanation":"Health phrasal verb, idiom or word family.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال المركبة والتعابير."},{"q":"","options":["Did you receeve the doctor's letter?","Did you resieve the doctor's letter?","Did you recieve the doctor's letter?","Did you receive the doctor's letter?"],"answer":"Did you receive the doctor's letter?","explanation":"Correct spelling.","explanation_ar":"التهجئة الصحيحة."},{"q":"","options":["Keep the medicine separate from the food.","Keep the medicine separete from the food.","Keep the medicine seprate from the food.","Keep the medicine seperate from the food."],"answer":"Keep the medicine separate from the food.","explanation":"Correct spelling.","explanation_ar":"التهجئة الصحيحة."},{"q":"Pick the best sentence for a health leaflet:","options":["Avoid staying up late, and try sleep at least eight hours.","Avoid stay up late, and try to sleeping at least eight hours.","Avoid staying up late, and try to sleep at least eight hours.","Avoid to stay up late, and try sleeping at least eight hour."],"answer":"Avoid staying up late, and try to sleep at least eight hours.","explanation":"Gerund or infinitive after a verb.","explanation_ar":"ing أم to بعد الفعل."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS5-IMG01","prompt":"A tri-fold leaflet \"Healthy Body, Healthy Mind\" on a desk with icons: a water drop, a plate with balanced food, a moon, a smiling brain; Noura and Sara folding copies for the school health week. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A tri-fold leaflet \"Healthy Body, Healthy Mind\" on a desk with icons: a water drop, a plate with balanced food, a moon, a smiling brain; Noura and Sara folding copies for the school health week"},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS5-IMG02","prompt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Healthy Body, Healthy Mind”, speech bubbles left empty. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Healthy Body, Healthy Mind”, speech bubbles left empty"},{"id":"GV-L06-U3-LS5-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Board Race Review”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Board Race Review"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U3-LS5-T1","script":"Taking care of your body and mind is easier than you think! First, try to drink at least six glasses of water a day. Staying hydrated helps you concentrate. Avoid skipping breakfast – a balanced meal gives you energy for the whole morning. If you enjoy playing sports, keep doing it! If not, start walking for twenty minutes after school. It's also necessary to cut down on screen time before bed. Instead of scrolling on your phone, read a book. When you feel stressed, talk to someone you trust. Remember: everyone feels under the weather sometimes. We definitely recommend sleeping eight to nine hours a night. You'll feel energetic and fit as a fiddle!","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U3-LS5-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Healthy Body, Healthy Mind: Our Class Leaflet – Language in Use”. Let’s learn gerunds and infinitives, -ing subjects and preposition + -ing, health phrasal verbs, idioms and word families, commonly misspelled words (unit review) together. Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Health talk show: in pairs, one student is a health expert, the other is a TV presenter. The presenter asks 5 questions (What do you suggest doing…? What should teenagers avoid…?). The expert answers with gerunds, infinitives, a phrasal verb and an idiom. Today you use all of Unit 3: gerunds and infinitives, -ing subjects, preposition + -ing, health phrasal verbs and idioms, word families and spelling. A health leaflet gives clear advice (try to…, avoid…, it's necessary to…), explains why (Staying hydrated helps…) and ends with encouragement. Here are some examples. Eating slowly helps your stomach. Try to stand up every hour. Avoid drinking energy drinks. Be careful! Some learners say: “Avoid to drink soda.” That’s not right. We say: “Avoid drinking soda.” avoid + -ing. Quick check: what is wrong with “Sleep early help you grow.”? … Think! … It should be “Sleeping early helps you grow.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can give health advice to my classmates.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.95"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"My sister enjoys ___ healthy smoothies.","options":["to make","made","making","make"],"answer":"making","explanation":"enjoy / avoid / finish / keep / mind / give up / suggest + -ing.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال + ing."},{"q":"We've agreed ___ sugary drinks at home.","options":["stop buying","to stop buying","stopping to buy","to stop buy"],"answer":"to stop buying","explanation":"want / decide / hope / promise / agree / plan / learn + to.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال + to."},{"q":"Please avoid ___ in the hospital corridors.","options":["run","running","ran","to run"],"answer":"running","explanation":"enjoy / avoid / finish / keep / mind / give up / suggest + -ing.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال + ing."},{"q":"","options":["The dentist told me brushing my teeth twice a day.","The dentist told me brush my teeth twice a day.","The dentist told to me brush my teeth twice a day.","The dentist told me to brush my teeth twice a day."],"answer":"The dentist told me to brush my teeth twice a day.","explanation":"advise / tell / ask / want + object + to.","explanation_ar":"الفعل + مفعول + to."},{"q":"I hope ___ my fitness test next week.","options":["passing","to passing","to pass","pass"],"answer":"to pass","explanation":"want / decide / hope / promise / agree / plan / learn + to.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال + to."},{"q":"___ the stairs is better than taking the elevator.","options":["Climbing","Climbs","Climb","To climbing"],"answer":"Climbing","explanation":"-ing form as the subject + singular verb.","explanation_ar":"ing فاعلًا."},{"q":"","options":["Doing puzzles keep your brain active.","Doing puzzles keeps your brain active.","To doing puzzles keeps your brain active.","Do puzzles keeps your brain active."],"answer":"Doing puzzles keeps your brain active.","explanation":"-ing form as the subject + singular verb.","explanation_ar":"ing فاعلًا."},{"q":"Always wash your hands after ___ the bathroom.","options":["use","used","using","to use"],"answer":"using","explanation":"Preposition + -ing.","explanation_ar":"حرف الجر + ing."},{"q":"I'm really looking forward to ___ the new sports center.","options":["trying","tried","try","be try"],"answer":"trying","explanation":"look forward to + -ing.","explanation_ar":"look forward to + ing."},{"q":"My cousin is interested in ___ a nurse.","options":["become","became","to become","becoming"],"answer":"becoming","explanation":"adjective + preposition + -ing (good at, tired of).","explanation_ar":"الصفة + حرف الجر + ing."},{"q":"The doctor told my uncle to ___ fatty food.","options":["cut down on","pass out","come down with","cut up"],"answer":"cut down on","explanation":"Choose the right health phrasal verb.","explanation_ar":"الفعل المركب الصحيح."},{"q":"My brother ___ the flu just before his exams.","options":["cut out","came down with","got over","came up with"],"answer":"came down with","explanation":"Choose the right health phrasal verb.","explanation_ar":"الفعل المركب الصحيح."},{"q":"\"Are you OK?\" – \"I'm a little ___ – just a headache.\"","options":["over the moon","under the weather","back on my feet","fit as a fiddle"],"answer":"under the weather","explanation":"Choose the idiom with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"التعبير الاصطلاحي."},{"q":"Before the final exam, Rakan ___ every night.","options":["burned the midnight oil","was under the weather","took it easy","was fit as a fiddle"],"answer":"burned the midnight oil","explanation":"Choose the idiom with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"التعبير الاصطلاحي."},{"q":"Yoga is a good form of ___.","options":["relaxing it","relax","relaxation","relaxed"],"answer":"relaxation","explanation":"Choose the right word-family form.","explanation_ar":"صيغة العائلة."},{"q":"Spinach is very ___.","options":["nutritious","nutrition","nutritiously","nutrient it"],"answer":"nutritious","explanation":"Choose the right word-family form.","explanation_ar":"صيغة العائلة."},{"q":"","options":["belive","believe","beleive","beleeve"],"answer":"believe","explanation":"i before e, except after c.","explanation_ar":"قاعدة ie."},{"q":"","options":["It's necesary to rest after an injury.","It's neccessary to rest after an injury.","It's neccesary to rest after an injury.","It's necessary to rest after an injury."],"answer":"It's necessary to rest after an injury.","explanation":"Double or single letters (necessary, recommend, occasionally).","explanation_ar":"الحروف المضاعفة."},{"q":"","options":["swimmming","swimeing","swimming","swiming"],"answer":"swimming","explanation":"Double the final consonant (stopping, beginning).","explanation_ar":"مضاعفة الحرف."},{"q":"In which word is one letter not pronounced?","options":["message","mouse","music","muscle"],"answer":"muscle","explanation":"Silent letters (muscle, stomach, knee).","explanation_ar":"الحروف الصامتة."},{"q":"","options":["I'll defenitely join the walking club.","I'll definitly join the walking club.","I'll definately join the walking club.","I'll definitely join the walking club."],"answer":"I'll definitely join the walking club.","explanation":"Commonly misspelled word.","explanation_ar":"كلمة شائعة الخطأ."},{"q":"Choose the best sentence for a health leaflet.","options":["Drinking water regularly helps you concentrate, so try to keep a bottle on your desk.","Drink water regularly help you concentrate, so try keeping a bottle on you're desk.","Drinking water regularly help you concentrate, so try to keeping a bottle on your desk.","Drinking water regularly helps you concentrate, so try keep a bottle on your desk."],"answer":"Drinking water regularly helps you concentrate, so try to keep a bottle on your desk.","explanation":"-ing form as the subject + singular verb.","explanation_ar":"ing فاعلًا."},{"q":"How can we fix it? \"i decided stopping drink soda becaus its unhealthy.\"","options":["i decided to stop drinking soda because it's unhealthy.","I decided stopping to drink soda because its unhealthy.","I decided to stop drinking soda because it's unhealthy.","I decided to stop drink soda because it's unhealthy."],"answer":"I decided to stop drinking soda because it's unhealthy.","explanation":"want / decide / hope / promise / agree / plan / learn + to.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال + to."},{"q":"What do you enjoy doing in your free time? – ___","options":["I'm enjoy cycling with my friends.","I enjoy cycle with my friends.","I enjoy to cycle with my friends.","I enjoy cycling with my friends."],"answer":"I enjoy cycling with my friends.","explanation":"enjoy / avoid / finish / keep / mind / give up / suggest + -ing.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال + ing."}],"theme_ar":"جسم سليم وعقل سليم","essential_question_ar":"ما العادات اليومية التي تحافظ على صحة أجسامنا وعقولنا؟","can_do":"I can talk about habits and health with gerunds and infinitives, use -ing forms as subjects and after prepositions, use health phrasal verbs and idioms, and spell commonly misspelled words correctly.","can_do_ar":"أستطيع أن أتحدث عن العادات والصحة باستخدام صيغة المصدر بـ -ing والمصدر بـ to، وأستخدم صيغة -ing فاعلًا وبعد حروف الجر، وأستخدم أفعالًا مركبة وتعابير اصطلاحية صحية، وأتهجّى الكلمات التي يكثر الخطأ فيها بشكل صحيح."});
